# The system statements a web page hands to its host's runtime hooks
# (D67, D69-D85, D96), at the top level and inside a function, which then
# becomes async.
to doAll path
    download file from "https://example.com/a.txt" to path
    run "notepad.exe" into proc
    run "calc.exe"
    run command "dir" over ssh to "me@host" into out
    run command "dir" on remote "host" using credential "c" into out2
    get processes into list
    for each p in list
        kill process p and its children
        set priority of process p to "high"
        wait for process p up to 5 seconds into done
        wait for process p up to 1 seconds
    .
    create symbolic link "l" pointing to "t"
    get symbolic link target of "l" into t
    get owner of "x" into owner
    set file "x" to read only
    set file "x" to writable
    get registry value "n" from "HKCU:\Software" into rv
    set registry value "n" to "d" in "HKCU:\Software"
    delete registry value "n" from "HKCU:\Software"
    get event log entries from "System" up to 5 into entries
    set credential "c" to "s"
    get credential "c" into secret
    delete credential "c"
    lock the computer
    sign out
    restart the computer
    shut down the computer
    print "f.txt" to "P"
    copy "x" to clipboard
    get clipboard into clip
    notify "T" with "M"
    get system information "os" into info
    choose file into f1
    choose folder into f2
    choose file to save into f3
    if file "l" is a symbolic link
        say "link"
    .
    if file "x" is read only and registry key "HKCU:\Software" exists
        say "ro"
    .
    return info
to plain
    say "nothing async here"
get system information "cpu" into cpu
get processes into all
get clipboard into clip
choose folder into place
say doAll "x.txt"
